{"beat": 5, "name": "CHAPTER 2 — THE TOP IS A STRETCH", "text": "Here's the part a good operator gets wrong even after the hill. The top isn't a point. The elasticity came with a range, -3.52 to -0.88, so the top is a stretch of hill, and a price move is a bet on where inside that stretch the top really is. So the honest question isn't what's the best price. It's what's the best step, given what we don't know. Run that across the whole catalog. 22 products have a usable fit. 2 were refused, because their price never moved enough to draw a line; the fit won't speak until the price has moved by 2% across 5 months, and on those products nobody ever moved it. Of the fitted ones, 22 have a move worth making. The best is TH-CASIRO-01: a 5.0% step to $37.84, expected to add $388 a month. The honest version is somewhere between $20 and $909, with a 4% chance it loses money. Every step is capped at 5%, because a small step you can read is worth more than a big step you can't. Across every move the catalog picks up about $1,701 a month in expectation. That's the sense in which your price is probably wrong. Not badly. Wrong by a step, on most products, in a direction you can only learn by measuring the slope.", "provider": "library", "words": [{"word": "Here's", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.29}, {"word": "the", "start": 0.313, "end": 0.383}, {"word": "part", "start": 0.418, "end": 0.72}, {"word": "a", "start": 0.789, "end": 0.859}, {"word": "good", "start": 1.01, "end": 1.265}, {"word": "operator", "start": 1.358, "end": 1.904}, {"word": "gets", "start": 1.962, "end": 2.148}, {"word": "wrong", "start": 2.194, "end": 2.519}, {"word": "even", "start": 2.589, "end": 2.786}, {"word": "after", "start": 2.833, "end": 3.065}, {"word": "the", "start": 3.111, "end": 3.181}, {"word": "hill.", "start": 3.228, "end": 3.599}, {"word": "The", "start": 3.878, "end": 3.994}, {"word": "top", "start": 4.052, "end": 4.272}, {"word": "isn't", "start": 4.331, "end": 4.563}, {"word": "a", "start": 4.609,